# GMS's 4 stands. Its 120x120 hitbox is one arrow's burst and it TRAVELS: the
# shot is aimed, so the box sweeps a platform rather than covering a patch of
# ground. The reach rule reads a box that stands somewhere -- see
# Skill.max_enemies.
#
# Two attacks out of one skill: the volley the player holds the key for, and
# the turret they leave behind firing by itself. One row in the book and one SP
# ladder, because it is one skill.
#
# The turret is a BUFF, not an auto mode. GMS installs it with the Interact
# key mid-cast and gives it u = 20+2x seconds, so it is something the player
# puts up, loses and puts up again -- and the 800ms install is theirs to pay.
# An auto mode has no clock of that shape: it would fire for the whole fight
# for nothing. See Buff.own_cast_delay_ms.
#
# Neither half answers to attack speed. The volley is a key-down skill, which
# GMS paces itself, and the turret is a summon, which nothing has ever hurried.
# So a Ranger gets nothing from Agile Bows, exactly as in GMS.
name: "Arrow Blaster"
description:
  "Shoot an arrow at a high angle, and set up an Arrow Blaster which fires "
  "arrows automatically."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_RANGER skill_order: 1 }
max_level: 20
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_BOW
base_delay_ms: 120
fixed_delay: true
max_enemies: 4
hits_per_attack_count: 7
base { skill_pct: 1.24 }
per_level { skill_pct: 0.03 }
buff {
  # GMS u = 20+2x with x the level, so 22 at 1 and 60 at 20.
  duration_seconds: 22.0
  duration_seconds_per_level: 2.0
  own_cast_delay_ms: 800
  pulse {
    label: "Turret"
    cast_interval_seconds: 0.21
    max_enemies: 4
    base { skill_pct: 0.66 }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.01 }
  }
}
